# Winter's Embrace — An Adventure at the Winter Court

**Version:** 0.4
**Source:** Legend of the Five Rings Roleplaying Game — Winter's Embrace (product L5R09)
**Publisher:** Fantasy Flight Games (2019)

> GM-facing narrative. Boxed **read-aloud** text is reproduced verbatim; intervening GM procedure is
> summarized faithfully — the full detail lives in the source PDF. The Dramatis Personae statblocks
> are in `l5r5e-0.4-winters-embrace-cast.ttrpg` and the act structure in `l5r5e-0.4-winters-embrace.arc`.
> This adventure uses the players' own Winter Court characters, so there are no pregens. The boxed
> product's calendar, character-reference sheet, and punchboard are components referenced here, not
> reproduced.

---

## Adventure Background

The year is **1122** of the Isawa Calendar. It has been two years since a terrible tsunami struck Crane lands, and one since a massive typhoon hit the southern coast; two successive failed harvests have quietly weakened the once high-and-mighty **Crane**, who must appear untroubled or invite the **Lion** to swoop in and reclaim the contested Osari Plains and city of Toshi Ranbo.

To that end, the Lion seek to drive a wedge between the Crane and the **Mantis**. The Crane and Mantis have strained relations — the Crane suspect the Mantis of pirate attacks on their coast, while the Mantis chafe at Crane traditionalism. The Lion's Ikoma family, through Ambassador **Ikoma Ujiaki**, means to inflame those tensions: an Ikoma shinobi, **Ikoma Rumiko**, disguised as a Kabuki actor, has **forged the Mantis' invitation** to this year's court. The Mantis, meanwhile, hope to seize the stage of the Winter Court to put one of their own — **Lady Magami**, niece of Lord Yoritomo — forward as a candidate for betrothal to the crown prince, against the traditional Crane candidate **Doji Chiyoe**.

This year, **Kyūden Doji** hosts His Imperial Majesty and his retinue, in part to celebrate the recent ascension of **Doji Hotaru** as Crane Clan Champion. The adventure represents a two-week span of a months-long proceeding — one of many schemes in play. It begins with an invitation to tea with the venerable Crane courtier **Kakita Ryoku**, who humbly asks the PCs to determine who invited the Mantis.

---

## Act I: Storms Roll Ashore

The PCs are tasked with finding out who invited the Mantis to the Emperor's court. Very few know how the invitation was sent, and those who do want the truth hidden; failing to uncover it costs the PCs a chance to raise their standing with Kakita Ryoku and the Crane.

### Day 1: A Tea Ceremony Fit for an Empress

Ryoku's letter — its brushwork legendarily fine, its washi flecked with white to evoke snowfall — invites the PCs:

> Fallen leaves blanket the ground. The sea breeze brings the chill of winter, and the nights grow long. Despite the cold, this season is a gift, as is the chance to forge new friendships. I wish to serve you a simple bowl of tea in an intimate gathering in the tradition of Lady Doji. I am greatly looking forward to receiving you at the floating teahouse on the fifteenth day of the Month of Togashi, at the Hour of the Horse. Please refer to the enclosed map to locate this humble teahouse. My apprentice, Doji Chiyoe, will receive you in the gardens.

At the floating teahouse, received in the gardens by her apprentice **Doji Chiyoe**, Ryoku charges the PCs with uncovering who invited the Mantis. Her stated duty (giri) is to keep the crown prince betrothed to Chiyoe; her true desire (ninjō) is to restore the Crane to power and, in the process, ruin **Bayushi Kachiko**. She trades further favors to PCs who assist her.

### Court Happenings

Across the first week, the PCs investigate amid the court's events — the **Game of Letters** (an ongoing exchange of coded correspondence), the **poetry competition** (overseen by the priest **Asahina Takako**, where Lady Magami makes her debut), and the many parties **Doji Hatsuhina** throws. With careful work, the PCs trace the forged invitation to **Ikoma Rumiko** — outwardly a gregarious Kabuki actor, secretly a Lion shinobi of the Ikoma Shadow School — and may capture her. As they do, they are swept into the greater intrigue: which clan's candidate will be the future Empress.

---

## Act II: The Tale of the Fisherman's Daughter

At a luncheon, Ryoku makes a new request: could the PCs arrange with the director **Doji Shigeru** for Lady Magami to take the leading role of **Doji Mioko** in the upcoming Kabuki production? The Emperor himself will attend, so Magami's performance will be his chief impression of her. Ostensibly Ryoku wants to help Magami — but there is an undertone to her words: *set Magami up, but set her up to fail.*

The play is *The Tale of the Fisherman's Daughter*. Its director, **Doji Shigeru**, performs female roles under the celebrated secret persona **Lady Shike**; **Ikoma Rumiko** is cast as the island spirit. Working through casting and rehearsal, the PCs shape Magami's debut before the Emperor — advancing or sabotaging the Mantis' bid for the future Empress — and decide where their loyalties fall between Crane tradition and Mantis ambition.

---

## The Court's Players and Their Schemes

- **Kakita Ryoku (Crane):** the legendary courtier and author of *Winter*, tasked by Chancellor **Kakita Yoshi** to keep the crown prince betrothed to Doji Chiyoe, and driven to disgrace the Mantis and ruin Bayushi Kachiko.
- **Doji Chiyoe (Crane):** Ryoku's devout apprentice and the Crane's Empress candidate — sheltered, naïve to peasant hardship, and secretly drawn to Perfect Land Sect philosophies.
- **Doji Hatsuhina (Crane):** deputy seneschal and party-host, bitter at **Otomo Koryusai** for casting aside their betrothal, and bent on flaunting a better catch to punish him.
- **Otomo Koryusai (Imperial):** an overworked bureaucrat, wed to **Bayushi Mikuru** but pining for Hatsuhina, whom he would do anything to win back.
- **Miya Satoshi (Imperial):** the Imperial Herald and Master of Ceremonies — secretly a **Kolat** agent who seeks to sow chaos, propping up the Mantis' bid to throw the Empire into turmoil; he lets the forged Mantis invitation stand and blames his subordinate Koryusai.
- **Ikoma Rumiko (Lion):** the shinobi who forged the invitation, working to keep the Lion's hand hidden and thwart the Crane.
- **Lady Magami (Mantis):** Yoritomo's niece, healed as a sickly child by a fire spirit, groomed for the crown prince; if betrothed, she would open Rokugan's borders with the Unicorn.
- **Lord Yoritomo (Mantis):** the Son of Storms, Mantis Champion, seeking to raise the Mantis from Minor to Great Clan, introducing his niece to all of great and good Rokugan.
- **Susano-o no Izen (Mantis):** Magami's loud, loyal Storm-Fleet advocate.

---

## Conclusion & Rewards

The standing of the Crane and Mantis — and the identity of the future Empress — turn on the PCs' choices. Suggested experience:

- **2 XP** each: uncovering the identity of the Mantis-invitation forger; acquiring a copy of the Mantis' invitation (stolen or not); uncovering the Mantis plot to marry Lady Magami to the crown prince before Day 8; placing in the poetry competition; capturing the shinobi.
- **1 XP** each: competing in the poetry competition; participating in *The Tale of the Fisherman's Daughter*; writing at least three letters as part of the Game of Letters (repeatable).

If run within a full Winter Court, this is an introductory intrigue with many plots left to unravel afterward.

---

## Tie-ins

*Winter's Embrace* pairs with *Courts of Stone* (more Winter Court material, and Doji Hotaru's court) and can be expanded with the free downloadable supplement **The Scroll or the Blade**, which adds a Dragon-Phoenix custody dispute overseen by the Imperial Herald **Miya Satoshi** and the matchmaker Shika Yuki during these same days. GMs may adjust the year (1122) to fit their campaign.
